WEBVTT

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.760
These are the coordinates!

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.730
My homeworld after five years!

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.600
Release the Cyberse!

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.630
There it is!  Cyberse World!

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.160
Just wait, everyone!

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.330
What?  Is this a joke?

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.260
Is everyone okay?

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.000
It's me!  Ai!

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.270
Wait, that's wrong.

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:57.740
Hey!

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:59.790
Anyone!

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.450
No way...  No one's here?

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:09.410
What happened?

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.120
Is someone here?

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:28.090
Linkuriboh...

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.570
There there.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.840
I'm glad you're okay.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:39.930
By the way...

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:42.450
Where did everyone go?

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:47.190
What happened to Cyberse World?

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:56.860
Linkuriboh...

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:00.420
If all you say is "kurikurilink"...

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.850
I can't understand you!

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:27.150
Our lives aren't forever

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:33.960
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:41.270
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:47.840
Sharing hope for the future

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:54.580
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:02:54.800 --> 00:03:01.820
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:08.530
I want to share your pain

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.290
It's three months since he left.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.740
Where did you go leaving me behind?

00:03:54.250 --> 00:04:00.790
If you look angry, you'll scare 
the customers away, Yusaku Fujiki.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.990
Aoi Zaizen...

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:04.990
Just passed by here by chance.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:07.760
You have a part-time job here?

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:13.520
I know the owner, so he put 
me in charge while he's away.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:14.710
I see.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:21.100
Thank you.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:24.480
You found me when I was unconscious.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:27.080
I never thanked you for that.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.950
It's fine.  Anyone would've done the same.

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:34.420
Can I have a hot dog and coffee?

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:37.090
You don't have to order.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:41.190
Oh?  Not sure if I should say this...

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.200
I don't think you'll get customers today.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:51.770
Mom, don't think of entering my room!

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:57.330
Here I go!

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.910
Into the VRAINS!

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:17.760
I'm in the new LINK VRAINS!

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.510
There's a lot of people!

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:23.940
A lot of events are going on!

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.850
A card shop and item shop!

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:29.040
Even a D-Board shop!

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.990
Lots of different stores.

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:36.880
What's with this crowd?

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:47.130
Blue Angel!

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:51.080
Everyone!  Are you enjoying 
the new LINK VRAINS?

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.740
There are a lot of events today!

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:01.650
I'll have fun too!

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:08.180
The new LINK VRAINS is a big success, Boss!

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:11.040
Yeah.  It's a complete reboot.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:13.280
Because it was badly destroyed...

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:16.520
So it's all thanks to the fight with Hanoi?

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:17.920
Don't be stupid!

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:20.230
We almost lost our lives!

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:21.990
Sorry.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.490
But today is a day of celebration.

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:26.200
I'll let that go.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:30.170
Lots of duels going on in the Event Area!

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:33.170
But the most popular way to duel is-

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:36.670
- Outta the way!
 - Front front front!  Look ahead!

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:43.450
The most popular is Speed Dueling.

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:48.720
In the new LINK VRAINS, the ban 
on Speed Duels has been lifted.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:49.960
Yeah.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:53.220
The upgraded D-Boards are easier to control.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:58.560
And the course boundaries have emergency 
restoration functions, so it's safer.

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:02.300
They don't need to play in secret anymore.

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:07.560
Looks like a fun city.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:10.780
There must be new treasures here.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:18.440
But what's most surprising is that 
Playmaker has a bounty on his head.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:26.560
Queen, why must we search for Playmaker?

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:31.910
Every since you were reinstated as Security 
Manager, you've become quite bold.

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:34.620
Your former staff were reassigned.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.540
You think you're free to do what you like?

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:43.530
The Knights of Hanoi have been destroyed, 
and the Cyberse World has been found.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:46.240
But the Ingis weren't there.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:50.180
It's only natural to recapture 
the Ignis from Playmaker.

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:50.670
But-

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:52.980
If the Ignis aren't found...

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:57.860
Our company's operations won't improve.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:04.200
Zaizen, I'm putting you in charge 
of the bounty hunter team.

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:06.370
Bounty hunter?

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:10.900
A special search team to capture 
Playmaker and the Ignis.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:15.910
Use them to capture the 
Ignis, whatever it takes.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:22.520
If you can't, you'll end 
up like your former staff.

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:32.050
Mr. Onizuka's team has arrived.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.560
Please enter.

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:41.100
Thanks for coming, Mr. Onizuka.

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:46.600
Akira Zaizen...  I never 
thought you would be my boss.

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:50.810
I can say the same, Mr. Onizuka.

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:55.310
I never thought you'd accept 
being my company's bounty hunter.

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:58.000
Everyone has their own reasons.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:02.690
Even if you're my boss, 
don't invade my privacy.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:09.140
I heard there was one more bounty hunter.

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:10.320
Where is he?

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.530
He hasn't arrived yet.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:17.640
What duelist would dare to keep me waiting?

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:20.170
He's a pro among pros.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:21.610
He's dangerous.

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:25.080
He hunts his prey without mercy.

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:31.670
Blue Angel was seriously great!

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:34.020
I'll definitely go to next week's event too!

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:46.460
So this is Central Station.

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:50.200
Excuse me.

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:52.940
Please go ahead.

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.670
Thank you, umm...

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:58.140
I'm Brave Max!

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:00.750
That's a strong-sounding name.

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:02.370
Thank you!

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:05.620
I'm Playmaker's best friend!

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:07.680
You are?

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:10.700
But you shouldn't say that.

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:13.820
There's a reward for capturing Playmaker.

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:16.170
Bounty hunters will arrive.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.700
Then I'll beat them away!

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:21.700
You're so dependable!

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:22.930
Good luck!

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:27.830
She's beautiful... but 
maybe not in real life.

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:32.190
But since she liked my account name, 
it definitely means she's beautiful!

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:35.650
A wonderful encounter must be ahead!

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:47.140
Wow!  This place has a lot of info!

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:50.360
For tomorrow's event, double 
points for Speed Duels!

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:54.830
Then let's search for cards today.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:59.380
This is the best place to learn 
LINK VRAINS' current state.

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:00.620
Out of the way!

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:02.810
Move!

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:05.250
This is our spot!

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:07.080
That's right!

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:08.550
It's a nice spot, bro.

00:11:08.990 --> 00:11:12.520
There's people like that everywhere.

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:15.250
Hey!  You move too!

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:18.960
Bro!  He's not moving!

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:20.960
Leave this to me!

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:26.900
Violence can't be performed in LINK 
VRAINS, but that doesn't apply to us.

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:29.690
We modded ourselves using illegal programs.

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:32.200
Take this!  Penguin Punch!

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.170
Let me go, punk!

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:39.150
I can also kill players.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:46.080
Bro!

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:47.940
He disappeared!

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:49.950
He's a bounty hunter!

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:54.390
You'll regret this!

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:58.360
Did he come here to find me?

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:01.830
You haven't changed, Blood Shepherd.

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:03.660
Ghost Girl.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:08.070
I heard SOL Technologies 
hired you as a bounty hunter.

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:10.940
Didn't they call you too?

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:14.350
But I don't intend to accept.

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:16.410
I owe Playmaker.

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:19.880
Owe or owed, you're too soft as usual.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:22.850
Unlike you, I don't make all 
my decisions based on money.

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:25.130
That's what makes me a pro.

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:26.500
But whatever.

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:28.930
Just don't interfere with me.

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:31.780
I won't show mercy, even for you.

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:46.020
Recently, he goes outside more.

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:50.480
Since his brother comes to visit, 
he's heading in a good direction.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:54.090
Because the incident that 
threatened him has ended.

00:12:54.570 --> 00:12:59.480
That info may have calmed him.

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:04.600
Jin, there's something I 
want to talk to you about.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:10.120
I have a small hot dog stand in Den City.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:13.810
If you'd like, want to live with me there?

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:18.580
I just want to be with you.

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:22.540
Jin?

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:28.790
Who are you?

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:31.620
Stop!  Stay away from Jin!

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:32.920
What?

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:49.440
Stop it!

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.380
Jin!  Jin!

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:02.820
What happened?

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:05.460
Oh hey, Kusanagi.

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:07.080
The store's fine...

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:08.790
What?

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:12.260
He escaped into LINK VRAINS!

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:14.600
Hurry up and capture him!

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.830
Deck set!

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.120
Into the VRAINS!

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:26.980
This is the new LINK VRAINS.

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:37.050
This is the new D-Board from Kusanagi.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:43.530
Where's the guy that Kusanagi mentioned?

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:45.450
Huh?  Wasn't that...

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:46.960
Playmaker showed up!

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:49.200
Let everyone know!

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:58.140
Playmaker has arrived!

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:04.820
Why is Playmaker here?

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:10.580
Where are you?

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:16.060
Found you, Playmaker.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:30.410
There's a bounty on your head.

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:33.140
I no longer have an Ignis.

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:35.370
You don't need to chase me-

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.150
Then what's that?

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:42.850
Sorry, Playmaker.  I came back.

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:44.820
Ai!  Why are you here?

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.830
I'll give a brief explanation.

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:48.860
So you see-

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:50.170
Save it for later!

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:53.250
Ah!  These feelings are coming back!

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:56.280
There he is!

00:15:56.730 --> 00:15:58.080
Who?

00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:01.010
He stole Kusanagi's brother's consciousness.

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:03.470
Things are crazy here too?

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:06.440
But before I go after him, I 
have to get rid of this guy.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:09.190
Okay!  Then let me show you this!

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:11.780
I've also updated!

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.100
Ta-daa!

00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:15.050
Releasing the Data Storm!

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:18.340
What?

00:16:19.970 --> 00:16:23.060
You're in danger.  Logging out.

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:26.000
All right!  Now's our chance!

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:31.740
What will you do next?

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:33.300
Challenge him to a duel.

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:38.310
In the new LINK VRAINS' duel 
rules, winners can make trades.

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:41.560
If I defeat him in a 
duel, I can get his data.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.050
You're right.

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:45.250
Defeat him.

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:46.980
Understood.

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:49.720
Looks like he wants to duel too.

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:54.360
I brought a gift.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.690
I found this in my homeworld.

00:16:56.900 --> 00:16:58.940
Put it in your deck!

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:04.670
I see.  It's not a bad card.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:05.770
Right?

00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:06.940
Here I go!

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:09.910
Speed Duel!

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:15.650
Boss, Playmaker has returned to 
LINK VRAINS after three months!

00:17:15.650 --> 00:17:18.050
I smell a big scoop!

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:20.290
After them, no matter what!

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:22.190
Okay!

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:25.890
My turn.

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:29.860
I set one card and end my turn.

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:34.100
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:39.720
I send a Cyberse in my hand to the 
graveyard to Special Summon Defcon Bird.

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:44.710
Then I Special Summon the Dotscaper 
that I sent to the graveyard.

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:48.780
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:52.620
The summoning condition 
is one Level 1 monster.

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:54.200
Link Summon!

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:56.930
Link 1 Linkuriboh!

00:17:58.280 --> 00:17:59.690
Good luck!

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:05.230
I summon Cyberse Wizard!

00:18:08.050 --> 00:18:11.640
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:15.880
The summoning conditions are 
two Level 3 or higher Cyberses.

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:17.340
Link Summon!

00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:19.900
Link 2 Elphase!

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:26.280
Elphase gains 300 ATK for every 
monster next to its link.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:30.690
Battle!  Go, Linkuriboh!

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:38.300
Then Elphase attacks you directly!

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:47.190
Does he really want to fight?

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:49.270
Will this be an easy win?

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:51.480
I end my turn.

00:18:51.820 --> 00:18:53.200
My turn.

00:18:54.010 --> 00:18:56.180
I summon High Drive Booster.

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:02.550
What's this sensation?

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:03.920
Is it from him?

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:06.160
No, this sensation...

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:08.390
That monster is a Cyberse.

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:14.280
Seriously?  Then it might have something 
to do with the Cyberse World's destruction.

00:19:14.280 --> 00:19:16.620
Cyberse World was destroyed?

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:18.740
We'll talk specifics later.

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:21.620
Don't let him escape, no matter what!

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:23.070
You don't need to tell me.

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:27.570
I activate the Continuous 
Trap, High Drive Generator!

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:31.310
I Special Summon a High Drive Token.

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:36.820
Appear!  The circuit that guides my path!

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:40.130
The summoning condition 
is one High Drive monster.

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:43.130
Link Summon!

00:19:43.130 --> 00:19:46.030
Link 1 Flow High Drive!

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:52.160
From my hand, I activate the 
Field Spell, Castle Link!

00:19:53.200 --> 00:20:00.440
Once per turn, I move a Link Monster to the 
Main Monster Zone that its link is pointing to.

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:03.410
What'll he do by moving 
the monster's position?

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:07.150
My Skill, Marker's Portal!

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:12.860
Once per duel, I can activate it when my LP 
are equal or lower than my original points.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:17.490
He only needed to take 
a little bit of damage.

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:20.430
Sheesh.  His dueling is so crude.

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:24.400
I activate one Link Spell from my deck!

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:26.110
Link Spell?

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:27.640
I never heard of that!

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:30.850
The card activated by this 
effect can't be negated...

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:33.610
...nor destroyed by your card effects!

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:37.920
I activate the Link Spell, Judgment Arrows!

00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:42.200
Only one Link Spell can be on my field.

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:47.090
It can only be activated in the Spell and 
Trap Zone next to a Link Monster's link.

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:50.830
Appear!  The circuit that guides my path!

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:52.800
Link Summon!

00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:55.980
Link 1 Flow High Drive!

00:20:56.780 --> 00:20:58.880
Hey, what's going on?

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:02.540
Why can he Link Summon in a 
spot without a Link Marker?

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:05.280
